d be worth creating an [issue there](https://github.com/awesome-gocui/termbox-go) mentioning this. For now, I'll submit a patch on FreeBSD bugzilla including the fixes and we can go from there.\n\nEdit: Report has been submitted on [bugzilla](https://bugs.freebsd.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=246486). As per standards, it'll await for review and will be merged when someone gets an opportunity to.","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1589553818,"nonce":"qlbXeP7d6D8dYI3IAwB9Cr0z280=","metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdElzc3VlQ29tbWVudEVkaXQ6MzcyNDY0MDY0"},"target":"a698d6b301c84da78799c14039a566f73ad4e9bfc64c89c34d86ddc529f2b670","message":"FreeBSD port maintainer for git-bug here.\n\nAs the go package [awesome-gocui](https://github.com/awesome-gocui/gocui) is using a custom fork of termbox, it's slightly outdated and hasn't inherited the FreeBSD [fixes from upstream](https://github.com/nsf/termbox-go/commit/58d4fcbce2a7e6a3a48afbc6b7ec2a916ac33ee0) and subsequently causing these issues you're experiencing. Since applying the patch aforementioned I'm no longer facing this issue, either:\n\n* Fixes are merged into the forked termbox awecome-gocui uses;\n* awesome-gocui switches it's custom fork to the upstream version.\n\nIn any case it would be worth creating an [issue there](https://github.com/awesome-gocui/termbox-go) mentioning this. For now, I'll submit a patch on FreeBSD bugzilla including the fixes and we can go from there.\n\nEdit: Report has been submitted on [bugzilla](https://bugs.freebsd.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=246486). As per standards, it'll await for review and will be merged when someone gets an opportunity to. If you want to try this fix locally, apply [this patch](https://bz-attachments.freebsd.org/attachment.cgi?id=214527) to the port and rebuild.","files":null}]}